Hey @smnandre! Thanks for the quick reply!

Sorting of the importmap entries was mentioned in the linked issue https://github.com/symfony/symfony/issues/65117#issuecomment-5164886082. Sorting the entries means to me putting them in alphabetical order. That would mean changes in the importmap of existing users after updating to a new version of Asset Mapper.

I would like to take this opportunity to refine the scope of this PR before moving further with the implementation.

1. Do we want to implement some kind of stable order?
2. What kind of order? Alphabetical or installation order?
3. Should we implement a configuration setting for this so the users can choose?

In my opinion, both order options have their merit. Letting the users have the freedom to choose their preferred one looks to me sensical. Defaulting to preserving the installation order would allow us to not make unnecessary changes in the importmap for the existing users.

